    <briefdescription>
<para>Each level of the interpreted policy is a vector which describes how the level is spread across the machine. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>For example, a level could be (128 threads), or it could be (4 blocks) x (32 threads). In the latter example, the level is described as a vector of 2 subentries. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
